3245,-0.05108855664730072,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.00200130813755095,-2.372236667724792e-05,-0.0021075436379760504,0.0,-1.4305104514278355e-06,-2.622600959512056e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"To solve for the sum of all possible values of \\( f(10^{100}) \\), we start by analyzing the given equation \\( g(f(x)) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) where \\( g(x) = x^2 - 11x + 30 \\).\n\nFirst, let's express \\( g(f(x)) \\) in terms of \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ g(f(x)) = (f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30. \\]\n\nWe know that:\n\\[ (f(x))^2 - 11f(x) + 30 = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42. \\]\n\nTo find \\( f(x) \\), we need to determine the roots of the polynomial \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\). Let's denote the roots of this polynomial by \\( r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4 \\). Then, we have:\n\\[ (f(x) - r_1)(f(x) - r_2)(f(x) - r_3)(f(x) - r_4) = x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42. \\]\n\nSince \\( g(x) = (x-5)(x-6) \\), it follows that \\( f(x) \\) must be one of the roots of the polynomial \\( x^4 - 14x^3 + 62x^2 - 91x + 42 \\) shifted by 5 or 6. Therefore, the possible values of \\( f(x) \\) are \\( r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4, r_1+5, r_2+5, r_3+5, r_4+5, r_1+6, r_2+6, r_3+6, r_4+6 \\).\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,70,2075,8,284,856,61,17,481,220,16,16,87,488,220,18,15,4779,323,1077,400,69,2075,15087,387,264,47311,1741,429,198,78045,70,955,2075,593,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,7110,60,9885,279,2629,315,678,3204,2750,315,400,69,7,16,15,47822,16,15,15,16630,3,151645,198,151644,77091,198,1249,11625,369,279,2629,315,678,3204,2750,315,17767,282,7,16,15,47822,16,15,15,5410,1124,701,582,1191,553,41018,279,2661,23606,17767,342,955,2075,593,284,856,61,19,481,220,16,19,87,61,18,488,220,21,17,87,61,17,481,220,24,16,87,488,220,19,17,1124,8,1380,17767,342,2075